 "title": "Each eigenvalue's Jordan blocks on the cut-open torus follow one polynomial's degree",
 "subject": "Networks of rings joined by shared contacts, read with the canonical knot test on their space-time law",
 "conclusion": "At sides 2^m the eigenvector G\u00b7Y^j heads a Jordan chain of exactly 2k \u2212 1 \u2212 4j, k = n/2 \u2212 deg G, at every eigenvalue to side 64 and nine of side 128 (computed), so an eigenvalue's multiplicity is read off its one polynomial's degree. Its first order is proved: the reduction is a Hankel matrix of G's norm, giving exactly k mod 2 blocks of size 1.",
